WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.444
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:07.037 --> 00:00:08.870
ALEXANDRINA GARCIA-VERDIN:
I love the quote,

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:10.460
"Stay in a learner's mind."

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:16.059
Because curiosity breeds the
desire to explore and to learn.

00:00:16.059 --> 00:00:18.970
And YouTube is a
fantastic resource

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:22.600
for exploring different
subjects and ramping up

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.750
on them, especially since
the tech sector is constantly

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:26.710
evolving.

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:28.543
TULSEE DOSHI: I think
one of the things that

00:00:28.543 --> 00:00:30.400
is really unique
about tech in general

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.205
is that it's so easy
to move between roles

00:00:33.205 --> 00:00:33.955
and between paths.

00:00:33.955 --> 00:00:35.500
And that can be both
in terms of the role

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:37.917
that you do-- so whether you
are an engineer, or a product

00:00:37.917 --> 00:00:39.495
manager, or a designer.

00:00:39.495 --> 00:00:41.620
But it can also be a move
between verticals, right?

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:44.650
So whether you work on Search,
or whether you work on Video,

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:48.040
or whether you work on
Machine Learning Products,

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:49.640
or UX heavy products.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:52.900
And so I would say
optimize for learning

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:54.490
and optimize for
what excites you.

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:57.220
And I think there is no such
thing as closing a door, right?

00:00:57.220 --> 00:01:00.610
So there is always opportunities
to return to a career path

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:01.400
that you like.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.650
There's always opportunities
to explore something new.

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:06.100
And every career path you
choose opens up a new door.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.470
RACHEL BEEN: There is so many
careers in technology that

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:11.180
haven't even been created yet.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:14.380
I came in to Google in
a job that didn't exist.

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:19.210
I was the first art
director on Android.

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:22.120
Some of my first jobs
were hiring illustrators

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:24.390
to create beautiful
artwork for Google Play.

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:26.410
That type of role
had never existed.

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:28.510
STEPHANIE WONG: Let
your curiosity lead you.

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:32.590
Even if your side passion might
be in the arts or humanities

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:33.610
space.

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:38.338
Allow that to infuse what you
end up doing in technology.

00:01:38.338 --> 00:01:40.630
RACHEL INMAN: So if you're
considering different career

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:42.430
paths in tech, I
would definitely

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:46.510
recommend thinking about what
really excites you, what really

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:49.510
gets your energy going, and
kind of matching that up

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:51.820
with where your skill sets lie.

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:55.060
SHILPA VIR: It depends on which
stage of career you are in.

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:58.960
If you are a student, try
to get different internships

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:03.370
and try something hands-on
to see if you like it.

00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:05.590
Talk to people in
those industries

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:08.440
about what their day
to day work looks like.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:10.699
See if you can
shadow some of them.

00:02:10.699 --> 00:02:14.020
See if you can do
some volunteering work

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:16.090
in that capacity for somebody.

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:18.932
And get some hands-on
experience to figure out

00:02:18.932 --> 00:02:20.390
if this is something
that you would

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:22.090
enjoy doing for the long term.

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:23.980
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
Explore, explore, explore.

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:25.500
Do not stop exploring.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:28.240
You will find that you can
match your current skills

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:31.660
with your passion, and really
create your own unique path

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:32.890
in tech that you love.

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:35.040
[MUSIC PLAYING]

